---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Page title="Privacy policy" eyebrow="Legal" description="How ronimichaeli.com handles your data: no tracking, no cookies, no forms." updated={site.updated}>
  <p>
    This website is the personal portfolio of {site.name}. Your privacy matters, so the site is built to collect as little as possible — in practice,
    nothing about you personally.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>No tracking cookies — so there is no cookie banner.</li>
    <li>No forms, accounts or newsletters — the site never asks for your personal details.</li>
    <li>No third-party fonts, embeds or CDNs — every file is served from this domain.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the <strong>Reduce motion</strong> switch in the footer, your choice is saved in your browser’s local storage under the key
    <code>rm-motion</code>, so the site remembers it on your next visit. It never leaves your device and you can clear it at any time from your browser
    settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on <a href="https://pages.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Pages</a>. Like any web host, GitHub
    may process technical data such as your IP address to deliver the pages and keep the service secure. See the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >GitHub Privacy Statement</a
    > for details. I do not have access to identifiable visitor data.
  </p>

  <h2>When you contact me</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose to write to me by email or WhatsApp, I receive the information you send — usually your name, contact details and message — and use it
    only to reply and to discuss work opportunities. I don’t sell or share it. Those messages are also subject to the privacy policies of your email
    provider and of WhatsApp.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    Project pages link to live products and to GitHub. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which this policy doesn’t cover.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the Israeli Privacy Protection Law and, where applicable, the GDPR, you may ask to see, correct or delete personal information you have sent
    me. Contact me via <a data-email={site.emailParts.join('|')} href="/#contact">email</a> and I’ll respond as quickly as possible.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page will be updated.</p>
</Page>
